WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.009
This is the Old Royal Naval College in
Greenwich. The World Heritage listed site

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:05.941
that most Americans and

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.719
let's be honest, most Brits, know as
 "that place that got blown up in Thor 2".

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:12.889
But that blowing up would have been a heck of a lot different

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:16.789
if it'd happened a couple of decades earlier. See for many years this was

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.220
a working Royal Navy training base. That's
why it's got the name: "Old Royal Naval College"

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.250
That's not centuries ago.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.670
There were sailors being trained here
up until the mid 90s.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.279
And, well, the Royal Navy has nuclear submarines.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:33.280
Nuclear submarines have nuclear reactors.
Nuclear reactors need people to run them

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.300
and so what do you do, if you are the Royal Navy and you need

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.440
sailors to run your nuclear reactors?

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.260
Well, you build a nuclear reactor in the
basement

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.700
of a 17th century building just miles
from the centre of London.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.100
Seriously, right here,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.289
somewhere in this complex, somewhere in the 
basement of this, the King William building,

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:57.100
there was a working nuclear reactor for
many years, from 1963

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.109
to the mid 90's. At the time when
Greenwich called itself a nuclear

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:04.360
free zone. This area was specifically
exempted.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.700
And, why was there no outcry? Well, first of all

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.930
not many people knew about it. The Royal Navy is
quite good at operational security

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:16.909
and secondly, well, despite the words
"nuclear reactor" being quite scary

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:21.509
it was only a tiny reactor. It produced
10 kilowatts that's enough to power

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:25.030
about five electric kettles. I mean the amount of fuel and waste it

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.200
produced are actually pretty tiny. There would
never have been

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.509
a Chernobyl here. But, well if Thor 
had invaded a couple of...

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:34.509
I don't know what Thor did, I-- I haven't seen the movie.

00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:37.600
If Thor would have invaded a couple of  decades earlier, who knows?

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.400
There might have been a bit more 
radioactivity, to power his hammer-

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:43.929
I-- like I said, I haven't seen the movie, I don't know what happened.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.560
This is the first videos powered
by the things you sent in. Thank you very much

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.180
David and Olly who tipped me off about the reactor in the middle of Greenwich.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.180
